      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Palace of Pena, a vivid example of Portuguese Romanticism, was begun by King‑Consort Ferdinand in the mid‑1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sintra",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sintra’s rapid 20th‑century growth was spurred by a rail link to Lisbon that brought summer travelers in droves.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sintra",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town inspired the board game Azul: Stained Glass of Sintra, named after the town in 2018.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sintra",
